# Walking Ballista's "This creature enters with X +1/+1 counters on it" is a replacement effect of its own (CR 614.1c). CR
# 614.12: which replacement effects apply to a permanent entering is judged on the permanent as it would exist on the
# battlefield, "taking into account ... continuous effects that already exist and would apply to the permanent". Humility
# ("All creatures lose all abilities and have base power and toughness 1/1") would take its abilities there, so the second
# Ballista, cast with X = 1 under Humility, enters with no counter: a 1/1 (Humility's base 1/1). The first, cast with X = 1
# before Humility (the positive control), has its counter and is 2/2 under Humility (base 1/1, the counter in layer 7c).

